WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:09.842
If we add a signal to itself, in phase, the amplitude doubles: a six decibel reinforcement.

2
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:19.159
With the inverted copy the sum is zero at every sample: total cancellation. That is why two microphones with inverted polarity can make a sound disappear.

3
00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:27.315
With a delayed copy, the result depends on the frequency. A delay of half a period cancels; a whole period reinforces.

4
00:00:28.018 --> 00:00:38.367
If the two frequencies are almost equal, the relative phase turns slowly and the sum swells and fades. These are beats: as many per second as the difference between the frequencies.
